<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keith Mitchell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keith Mitchell is a Grenadian politician and former mathematics lecturer who led the New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> and was Prime Minister of Grenada from 1995 to 2008 and again from 2013 to 2022, the longest tenure in the country's history. His governments faced the destruction caused by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-ivan">Hurricane Ivan</a> in 2004 and a long debt crisis, and he lost office to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dickon-mitchell">Dickon Mitchell</a>'s National Democratic Congress in 2022.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/keith-mitchell.jpg" alt="Keith Mitchell" width="267" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Foreign and Commonwealth Office · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keith_Mitchell.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
